# Request — the owner's collection preference. ``enabled`` false stops everything that
# adds to the record: enrolment, the scribe, descriptions and template learning. People
# already on file go on being recognized, and when and where they were seen is still noted
# so their retention clock counts from the last recognition. The setting persists in the store.
# No idempotency key or decided-on stamp: setting a flag to a value is idempotent by
# nature, and it names nobody, so there is no snapshot to have decided on.
bool enabled
---
bool success
string message
